A lacuna's target path ("cuont", line 10 of 1.0) isn't declared by schema 1.0.
checkLacunas finds it in Go and positions the error at the authored lacuna
(line 8), not at the path.
-- ship/history/0.0.thema --
schema: {
	title: string
	count?: int
}
-- ship/1.0.thema --
schema: {
	title: string
	count: int & <10
}

forward: {
	count: from.count
	lacuna: {
		kind: "Placeholder"
		target: "cuont"
		message: "count is a placeholder"
	}
}

backward: {
	count: to.count
}
-- out/error --
lens 0.0->1.0, lacuna 0: targetFields[0]: path "cuont" is not declared by schema 1.0:
    ship/1.0.thema:8:2
-- out/positions --
lens 0.0->1.0, lacuna 0: targetFields[0]: path "cuont" is not declared by schema 1.0
	authored ship/1.0.thema:8:2
